  "description": "Attack patterns for the original Digimon Pendulum. The wire carries five rounds of weak (1 damage) or strong (2 damage).\n\n`patterns` is indexed by the pre-battle charge -- the RAW shake count from Count Match Classic, 0-40, not the banded 0-3 quality the rest of the game uses. A real device announced effort 0 alongside a strong round, which is what rules Effort out as the source. An empty meter is five weak rounds and a full one the five strong ones the document's Ikkakumon sends; the ramp between, and which rounds turn strong within a band, are ours.\n\n`enemy_patterns` is for adventure battles, where the enemy has no charge to play: it reads the enemy's stage instead, Baby I all weak through Super Ultimate all strong.",
